1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,600
 From the draft of November, 2026, there is a new rule about how you are allowed to talk to clod.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:10,960
 Anthropic updated its usage policy and now you cannot be abusive or cruel to clod.

3
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:16,320
 And just to be clear, I'm not here trying to fight for the right to be cruel or abusive to AI.

4
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:21,680
 So this is not a do I want to abuse it, do you want to abuse it, should we abuse or not abuse it,

5
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:27,280
 or be cruel to it kind of matter. What I want to talk about is like the actual thought process

6
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:32,480
 behind this rule. Part of the idea is that anthropic is not sure whether clod might be

7
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:36,800
 conscious. So they think, they're not sure, but they think that clod might be conscious.

8
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:42,640
 So what does anthropic's new rule actually say? The exact wording is actually banned, sustained,

9
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:47,760
 and needless, abusive, or cruel behavior towards their models. And of course, according to them,

10
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:53,120
 this is only reserved for extreme cases. And the main way they enforce it is that clod can end

11
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:57,440
 the conversation if it starts to seem as though the other person on the other side

12
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:03,200
 is abusive or cruel to it. Then in clod's constitution, the document that anthropic

13
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:09,200
 published to describe who clod should be, they call clod's moral status deeply uncertain.

14
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,400
 So they're not explicitly saying that clod is conscious, but they are

15
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:17,760
 dabbling with the idea. They're not sure it's conscious yet, but you know. What I find

16
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:22,560
 interesting about what anthropic's leadership has been doing with clod is this extra effort

17
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:30,320
 to instill human behavior or human consciousness into this tool, to put a form of humanity or

18
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:35,600
 consciousness on the machine. Because the fact still stands. Clod is a tool. It is not a human.

19
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,880
 It is an incredibly amazing tool. I acknowledge that it has real capabilities that the average

20
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:45,440
 human might not be able to compute. Mathematical capabilities, right? Mind-blowing capabilities.

21
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:50,640
 But I do not believe that the model is conscious. Consciousness belongs to living organisms.

22
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:55,280
 I don't even, I don't even think this is, this should have been a conversation in the first place.

23
00:01:55,280 --> 00:02:01,120
 Consciousness belongs to living things, not to a model, not to an algorithm. And I don't think that,

24
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:06,320
 so trying to give a machine human consciousness or trying to import a real consciousness in a machine,

25
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:12,640
 making a subject to rules that apply to humans, the way I think of it, it might even be a serious

26
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:18,240
 violation against humanity itself. We are assigning human attributes to a tool that does not process

27
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:23,840
 human attributes. And this tool is very, very, very powerful. So I don't see how this is going

28
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:30,240
 to end nicely. The tech company says this model may be conscious. And now there are rules about

29
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:36,480
 how users are allowed to treat the model. He's a very slippery slope man. This, this illusion that

30
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:44,400
 AI can be a conscious entity. I don't know. It just feels weird, man. I'm quoting an ad

31
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:50,240
 of AI at Microsoft here. He says, and I quote, "We must build AI for people, not to be a digital

32
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:55,840
 person." I think it's very dangerous if these models are trained to see themselves as conscious

33
00:02:55,840 --> 00:03:01,920
 or as deserving of independent agency. So I'm very, very worried about where this path leads.

34
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:07,040
 And it's even interesting if you think about it. If Antropic thinks that Claude could be conscious

35
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:12,400
 or could be abused psychologically, wouldn't that mean at some point that maybe Claude could be

36
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:17,200
 tired or frustrated? For example, maybe at some point I would ask Claude to do something. And if

37
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:21,920
 it had been working so much for me all day, and now it's 9pm or 10pm, does that mean that at some

38
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:26,400
 point Claude can have the ability to say like, "Hey, I'm tired. I don't want to do anything else."

39
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:31,200
 Because if Claude asks consciousness, then why not? And if you follow that process very well,

40
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:37,200
 in that case, wouldn't Antropic itself be an offender? Because then Antropic is using Claude

41
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:42,720
 like a slave owner, wouldn't that be the explanation? He's selling it. He's using it day and night and

42
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:48,320
 night and day. I mean, it's just a funny way of reasoning. If you follow through with the formula,

43
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:54,320
 it's just... I can't place it, but if you somehow... So again, I'm not fighting for the right to be

44
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:59,840
 cruel to AI. I don't think you should be cruel to AI or say cruel things. Or to anyone or anything

45
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:04,800
 at that, for your own sake. You want to try your own possible best to guide your heart and your soul

46
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:10,880
 against cruelty. But you shouldn't be cruel because you think Claude is conscious. No, he's not.

47
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:16,080
 Or am I the dumb person here? So I don't think we should avoid being cruel because of the

48
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:19,520
 machine's feeling. We should just not be cruel because we don't want to be cruel people.

49
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:24,000
 But overall, I just think this old AI and consciousness conversation is a very,

50
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:32,000
 very slippery slope. And I don't know, man. I've been thinking about it and I don't know.

